# Angular Conventions

- Angular 22, standalone components only (no `NgModule`), zoneless (no `zone.js`).
- `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` on every component.
- `inject()` instead of constructor injection.
- Signal APIs: `input()`, `output()`, `model()`, `viewChild()`, `computed()`. Use `effect()` only for side effects that cannot be derived.
- Built-in control flow: `@if`, `@for` (always with `track`), `@switch`. No `*ngIf` / `*ngFor`.
- Routes are lazy (`loadComponent` / `loadChildren`); guards, resolvers and interceptors are functions. Route params reach components through `withComponentInputBinding`.
- File names follow Angular CLI 22 defaults: kebab-case, named by content (`task-card.ts`, `board-store.ts`, `tasks-api.ts`).

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
@Component({ selector: 'app-task-card', templateUrl: './task-card.html' })
export class TaskCard {
  @Input() task!: Task;
  @Output() edit = new EventEmitter<Task>();
  constructor(private store: BoardStore) {}
}

// ✅ GOOD
@Component({
  selector: 'app-task-card',
  templateUrl: './task-card.html',
  changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,
})
export class TaskCard {
  readonly task = input.required<Task>();
  readonly edit = output<Task>();
}
```

## Forms

- Typed Reactive Forms with `nonNullable` controls. Validators mirror the API: title 3–200, description ≤ 2000, password ≥ 8, due date not in the past only when changed.
- Labels on every control; errors linked via `aria-describedby`.

## UI and styling

- Build UI on Angular CDK (`Dialog`, `Overlay`, `DragDrop`, `A11yModule`); no component library.
- Tailwind v4 utilities over theme tokens (CSS custom properties). Never write raw hex colors in templates or component styles.
- Dark theme accent text/icons use the accent-text token (`#c179b9`), not `#a42cd6`.
- Red only for danger, errors and overdue, always with icon and text.
- Icons from `@lucide/angular` (not `lucide-angular`).
- Logo: full logo on the auth card, wordmark at the top of the sidebar, symbol for favicon and mobile header. Use the optimized app assets, never the originals in `docs/design/`. Logo colors are a brand asset, exempt from the palette rule. Do not alter the logo without asking.
- UI text is Brazilian Portuguese; code identifiers are English.
